## Issues

- [ ] `description` is ~458 chars (cap 200) — packs the runtime tool scope,
  the closed `kind` enum, the verbatim-bytes contract, and the negative-shape
  list (no `backend`, no `connector`, no `name`). Trim.
  Traces to: `description` field | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content (exact strings)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `intent` is ~224 words (cap 100). Restates description with added
  paragraphs about live-vs-seed, on-demand-only invocation, status branch
  shape. Trim.
  Traces to: `intent` field | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `outcomes.desired` has 12 items (cap 4); each is paragraph length and
  encodes type-system / schema-level invariants: response shape exactly
  `{ status, instructions }`, closed `kind` vocabulary, verbatim-section-bytes
  on `ok`, fixed-remediation-prose on each non-ok branch, single
  `parseBrainAide` call per `ok` invocation, status-vocabulary-mirrors-`BrainState`.
  Most are unit-testable.
  Traces to: `outcomes.desired` | Brevity Contract caps + outcomes-purpose test
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Forbidden-content

- [ ] `outcomes.undesired` has ~13 paragraph-length items enumerating retired
  regressions (registry dispatch, seed-section exposure under any `kind`,
  schema-level `kind` rejection bypass, response-shape discriminants,
  description-vs-handler drift). Forbidden content.
  Traces to: `outcomes.undesired` | Brevity Contract caps + Forbidden content
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] `## Context` is ~500 words (cap ~150). Recapitulates the live-vs-seed
  split, the response-shape partition, the on-demand-only-invocation rule.
  Most duplicates project root.
  Traces to: `## Context` | Brevity Contract caps + Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity, Sibling-redundancy

- [ ] `## Strategy` has 6 paragraph-length decisions (cap ~5 ≤80 words). Each
  encodes schema-level enforcement, response-shape stability, kind-agnostic
  remediation prose, single-parse-per-call rule, defensive-fallback rule.
  Traces to: `## Strategy` | Brevity Contract caps
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Brevity

- [ ] `## Good examples` and `## Bad examples` reproduce TypeScript handler
  bodies, exact JSON return shapes with all string fields filled, exact
  remediation prose strings. Cap is 2-3 brief; forbidden content saturated.
  Traces to: examples sections | Forbidden content (TypeScript code, exact strings)
  Misalignment: spec-bloat
  Category: Forbidden-content

- [ ] Sibling redundancy with project root: the live-vs-seed split, the
  closed-`kind` enum, the verbatim-bytes invariant, the response-shape
  partition, the no-registry-dispatch rule are all restated from parent.
  Traces to: outcomes, Strategy, Bad examples | Sibling-redundancy
  Misalignment: spec-gap
  Category: Sibling-redundancy

## Retro

aide_brain spec is bloated because the strategist treated every defense
against connector-dispatch as needing both an outcome and a Bad example.
The schema-level rejection of unknown `kind` values is unit-testable. The
verbatim-bytes invariant is unit-testable. The response-shape stability is
unit-testable. The spec should commit to "agent-facing brain entry point;
returns the live section bytes verbatim or a fixed remediation; closed
two-value `kind` enum" and let unit tests own the rest.
